  </div>

  <h2 id="proof">Build proof before you commit years to one specialization</h2>

  <p>
    Almost every paramedical specialization rewards visible proof of interest and understanding before you have a formal credential — admission interviews and early internship placements both notice it. These small tasks are for testing genuine interest and building a first entry in your skill portfolio; they do not replace the accredited degree, supervised clinical hours, or NCAHP registration that the profession legally requires, as covered above.
  </p>

